WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.662
The third response is a different
certified service for the workload.

2
00:00:03.662 --> 00:00:06.171
Chapter 10 works through collaboration,

3
00:00:06.171 --> 00:00:10.376
and its first rule is to read the
certification, not the announcement.

4
00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:14.345
On the Marketplace, Google
Workspace is certified at Class D.

5
00:00:14.345 --> 00:00:18.156
Gemini for Government is a
separate listing at Class B, Low,

6
00:00:18.156 --> 00:00:23.238
even though Google says Gemini in
Workspace apps is FedRAMP High authorized.

7
00:00:23.238 --> 00:00:28.163
Which AI features sit inside which
certification is a question for the package.

8
00:00:28.163 --> 00:00:33.914
And the Workspace listing marks some services
as not meeting a control enhancement,

9
00:00:33.914 --> 00:00:37.200
SA-9 five, on where processing
and storage happen.

10
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.812
Details like those decide
what you can turn on.

11
00:00:39.812 --> 00:00:42.162
The public record shows both outcomes.

12
00:00:42.162 --> 00:00:48.055
In September 2025 a cabinet-level department
awarded a five-year agreement worth up

13
00:00:48.055 --> 00:00:53.358
to 89 million dollars to move more than
50,000 employees to Google Workspace,

14
00:00:53.358 --> 00:00:57.988
under a GSA agreement with a
temporary 71 percent price reduction.

15
00:00:57.988 --> 00:01:02.912
So a five-year cost model has to price
the renewal years, not the launch price.

16
00:01:02.912 --> 00:01:07.286
A military department went the
other way, ending about 150,000

17
00:01:07.286 --> 00:01:12.001
Google email licenses after an
audit found about 16 percent in use.

18
00:01:12.001 --> 00:01:15.362
Adoption has to be measured
in the pilot, not assumed.

19
00:01:15.362 --> 00:01:19.162
The choice is only safe if
the identity plane stays put.

20
00:01:19.162 --> 00:01:24.359
Entra ID remains the source, and the suite
is a workload that consumes identity:

21
00:01:24.359 --> 00:01:28.837
provisioned, federated, with
Conditional Access applied at sign-in.

22
00:01:28.837 --> 00:01:30.438
Then close two gaps.

23
00:01:30.438 --> 00:01:33.587
Google super administrators
sign in outside it,

24
00:01:33.587 --> 00:01:37.288
and Google's own directory is
derived, so report its drift.

25
00:01:37.288 --> 00:01:41.387
The sponsor and CIO decide
which services the agency uses.

26
00:01:41.387 --> 00:01:46.302
Make the suite decision its own approval,
separate from identity modernization,

27
00:01:46.302 --> 00:01:49.220
and read the listing again
on the day you decide.
